  },
  "body": "## Cause\r\n\r\nThe work envelope (#1567, commit `c0b4dfc85`) does not move the camera target. No line puts it there:\r\n\r\n- The envelope is overlay lines only: `crates/ui/src/work_envelope.rs` `envelope_lines`, added to `interact::collect_overlay` (`crates/ui/src/interact.rs:947`).\r\n- `State::frame_all` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs:3847`) reads only the facets of named entities and the WCS origins. It does not read the overlay or the machine.\r\n- `Camera::orbit` turns about `Camera::target`. Only `frame_all`, pan, the wheel dolly and `actions::frame_at` write the target.\r\n\r\nThe pivot that the maintainer saw is the target that a document open left in place. `State::reset_for_open` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs:4225`) did not touch the camera. After an open, the target stayed at the old document's target, or at the default target at the world origin. No commit changed this; it is the same in v0.20.0. With a machine mounted, the envelope box is drawn about the work origin, near that target. Thus the orbit looked as if it turned about the envelope and not about the part.\r\n\r\nThe new test reproduced this before the fix: after an open, the target stayed at the parked `[400, 400, 400]`, with the envelope display on and off.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\n`reset_for_open` now calls `frame_all`, as the F key does. This applies to the disk open and the browser-bytes open (#1613). The status line still says `opened ...`. The envelope stays out of each camera bound.\r\n\r\n## Answers to the brief\r\n\r\n- The envelope display is off by default (`show_work_envelope: false`). With the box off, the envelope draws nothing and has no effect on the target. With the box on, it also has no effect on the target. The defect showed with the box on and off.\r\n- Other bodies, checked against `frame_all`:\r\n  - Fixtures and vises: they are facet entities, so they enter the frame. They did before #1567 too. They are physical bodies that the collision check reads, not display-only bodies. No change.\r\n  - Machine table: the viewport draws no machine table body. Nothing to check.\r\n  - Simulation tool body, toolpaths, height planes, the envelope: overlay or GPU parts only, not in the frame bounds.\r\n- The orbit about the point under the pointer is not in this PR. It is filed as #1998 (enhancement, P6, effort:medium).\r\n- #1963 and #1993 (envelope position and shape) are not touched.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\nIn the default ui lib suite, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/camera_target.rs` (value tests, no pixel snapshot):\r\n\r\n- `frame_target_is_the_same_with_the_envelope_on_and_off`: a mill with an asymmetric travel box is mounted. The frame target and distance are equal with the envelope on and off, and the target lies on the part and stock.\r\n- `open_frames_the_part_with_the_envelope_on_and_off`: a saved document is opened with the camera parked far away. The target after open is equal with the envelope on and off, lies on the part and stock, and is equal to the F-key frame. Failed before the fix.\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`): green, 1.0 min. ui lib 818 passed (6 ignored), and the suites boundary, boundary_picks, feedback, fixtures, gpu_render, machine, models, operations, shell, sinker_setup, theme_files all passed.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- No GUI hand test. The orbit drag on a real window was not tried.\r\n- No pixel snapshot lane (release only). No PNG changed.\r\n- The camera after File > New and after an import is unchanged by this PR.\r\n\r\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1997-envelope-camera-target.md`.\r\n\r\nEffort: high (no escalation).\r\n\r\nChangelog: A document open now frames the camera on the opened part and stock, so the orbit turns about the part and not about the old view's target.\r\n\r\nFixes #1997\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n\r\nMethod: an offscreen render of the real viewport (the test GPU path). No app window was opened. The project has a small part and a Tormach 770M, with the work envelope shown. Steps are the same before and after: open the project, then turn the camera by a fixed yaw of 0.9 rad.\r\n\r\nBefore (origin/main, cda3d5896). The camera stays at the default target (0, 0, 0) with distance 80. The part is not framed.\r\n\r\nView right after open:\r\n\r\n![before: after open](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/a1eedbe28cf583e499f658b6958b6750fcafabf1/pr-2000/open-before.png)\r\n\r\nView after the fixed orbit:\r\n\r\n![before: after orbit](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/a1eedbe28cf583e499f658b6958b6750fcafabf1/pr-2000/orbit-before.png)\r\n\r\nAfter (this PR, e2d0797e9). The camera frames the part and stock. The target is (0, 0, 10) and the distance is 277.\r\n\r\nView right after open:\r\n\r\n![after: after open](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/a1eedbe28cf583e499f658b6958b6750fcafabf1/pr-2000/open-after.png)\r\n\r\nView after the fixed orbit. The part stays in the centre:\r\n\r\n![after: after orbit](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/a1eedbe28cf583e499f658b6958b6750fcafabf1/pr-2000/orbit-after.png)\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
